  join us at 11:40 AM for lunch\, prior to the seminar.  The Fall Seminar S
 eries continues through December\; see our Fall Seminar Series page for sp
 eakers and topics. Sign up for our newsletter for announcements. \n\nAbout
  the Seminar:\n\nAs AI becomes woven into our daily lives and social insti
 tutions\, we are becoming “cyborgs\,” extending our minds and capabili
 ties through technology. But greater technological capability does not aut
 omatically lead to greater human flourishing. How can we design AI that st
 rengthens our ability to learn\, create\, connect\, and make thoughtful de
 cisions? In this talk\, I will introduce an interdisciplinary approach to 
 building AI systems and studying their effects on people. Through personal
 ized AI prototypes and large-scale experiments\, my research explores how 
 AI can both enhance and undermine human decision-making\, well-being\, rel
 ationships\, and sense of self. This work combines design\, engineering\, 
 and qualitative and quantitative research to advance a science of human-AI
  interaction grounded in human flourishing. I will also explore how resear
 ch can translate into real-world impact: from an AI digital twin that supp
 orts long-term thinking and has reached users in more than 100 countries\,
  to research that has helped shape legislation protecting children from co
